00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:20,285
Boy, have we got a vacation for you...

2
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:34,571
Westworld is a adventure, science fiction, western
film directed by Michael Crichton.

3
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
Delos is a futuristic amusement park that features themed
worlds populated by human-like androids.

4
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:03,142
After two patrons have a run-in with a menacing gunslinger in West World, the androids
at Delos all begin to malfunction, causing havoc throughout the park.

5
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:17,428
The Gunslinger, played by Yul Brynner.

6
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Peter Martin, played by Richard Benjamin.

7
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
John Blane, played by James Brolin.

8
00:33:54,285 --> 00:34:00,285
Medieval Knight, played by Norman Bartold.

9
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Chief Supervisor, played by Alan Oppenheimer.

10
00:42:22,857 --> 00:42:28,857
Medieval Queen, played by Victoria Shaw.

11
00:46:37,142 --> 00:46:43,142
Westworld is a 1973 American science fiction Western film
written and directed by Michael Crichton.

12
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
The film follows guests visiting an interactive amusement park containing
lifelike androids that unexpectedly begin to malfunction.

13
00:55:05,714 --> 00:55:11,714
The film stars Yul Brynner as an android in the amusement park, with
Richard Benjamin and James Brolin as guests of the park.

14
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
The film was from an original screenplay by Crichton and was his
first theatrical film as director, after one TV film.

15
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
It was also the first feature film to use digital image processing to
pixellate photography to simulate an android point of view.

16
01:07:48,571 --> 01:07:54,571
Critical reception was largely positive by contemporary and retrospective critics
and Westworld was nominated for Hugo, Nebula, and Saturn awards.

17
01:12:02,857 --> 01:12:08,857
Westworld was followed by a sequel, Futureworld (1976), and a
short-lived television series, Beyond Westworld (1980).

18
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
A television series based on the film debuted in 2016 on HBO.

19
01:20:31,428 --> 01:20:37,428
The film explores themes of future, android, man vs machine, saloon, old town.

20
01:24:45,714 --> 01:24:51,714
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
